sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-18> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch10-18--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch10-18--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch10-18: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.58" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.584"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Formula size after a few steps is a finite computation, and the contrast with rules 90 and 254 is well defined. Those small-n sizes can be recomputed and either continue the rapid growth Wolfram reports or break it. They do not prove that no simple formula exists for arbitrary step counts, nor the further claim about most cellular automata." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compute minimal disjunctive-normal-form and Nand formula sizes for the state of rule 30 after t steps, and compare growth with rules 90 and 254. Rapid growth relative to those rules at accessible t supports the small-n evidence; a compact formula at large t, or slow growth, would refute 'no simple formula'." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Exact minimal formulas become intractable as the light-cone width grows, so only small step counts are feasible.", "Growth of one normal form does not rule out a compact formula in some other language." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch10-18--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch10-18--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch10-18--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch10-18 by Grok 4.7: 0.68" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.68"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch10-18--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-18> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch10-18--grok--operationalizability> .
